@startuml seq-egress-injection
title Egress credential injection — DESIGNED vs DEPLOYED

box "DEPLOYED TODAY (F6/F9)" #FFE4E4
participant "hand h-<sid>\n(holds the credential)" as hand1
participant "worker NAT" as nat
end box
participant "GitHub / API" as ext1

hand1 -> hand1 : read ~/.git-credentials\n(pulled via grant; in memory + snapshot)
hand1 -> nat : HTTPS + Authorization, no inspection
nat -> ext1 : source = worker IP
note over hand1 #FFE4E4
  Secret lives inside the sandbox that runs
  model-generated code. No allowlist, no per-call
  audit, no central rotation. <b>Any</b> destination reachable.
  <b>F6</b>: it is also in every checkpoint of this actor.
end note

== ================================================== ==

box "DESIGNED (egress/, proof passed locally — NOT on cluster)" #E4FFE4
participant "hand h-<sid>\n(holds NOTHING)" as hand2
participant "egress gateway\n(TLS-terminating, internal CA)" as prox
end box
participant "vault (Secret Manager)" as sm2
participant "GitHub / API" as ext2

group pure injection (preferred)
  hand2 -> prox : HTTPS CONNECT, <b>no credential at all</b>
end
group placeholder swap (F12 — when the client demands a credential)
  hand2 -> prox : request carrying an <b>opaque placeholder</b>\n(git/CLIs will not call without one)
end
prox -> prox : identify caller\n(v1: per-session pairing;\nv2: Substrate ActorIdentity mTLS)
prox -> prox : destination allowlisted?
alt not allowlisted
  prox --> hand2 : <b>403 egress denied by policy</b>
else allowlisted
  prox -> sm2 : fetch that user's secret for this destination
  prox -> ext2 : re-originate + <b>inject Authorization</b>\n(swap placeholder -> real secret if present)\n(+ idempotency key for unsafe methods)
  ext2 --> prox : response
  prox --> hand2 : response
  prox -> prox : audit line: who / where / when
end
note over hand2 #E4FFE4
  Secret never enters the sandbox. One controlled
  egress point: allowlist, DLP, per-call audit,
  central rotation, per-user attribution.
  Policy comes from the AgentSpec (#29/#30) — declared
  today, <b>consumed by nothing</b>: no gateway is deployed.
end note

note over hand2, prox #FFE4E4
  <b>F11 — how traffic REACHES the gateway decides whether any of this holds.</b>
  HTTPS_PROXY env (the v1 proof): the sandboxed code can <b>unset it</b>
  and leave via the worker NAT — cooperative, not containment.
  atunnel (the fix): nftables redirect on the HOST, below the sandbox,
  mTLS + authenticated actor identity. The actor cannot switch it off.
end note
@enduml
